    description: "WI-tubot aggregate-v5 analysis (2026-04-16): kafka_streams_internal = 2386 candidates (2.6% of the pool). Top samples: KStream.process, KStream.filter, KStream.map, WorkerManager.Worker.spec, Utils.require.\n\nCurrent state: no linker covers Kafka Streams topology dispatch. The DSL (StreamsBuilder.stream().filter().map().through().to()) registers processors/transformers/suppliers at build time; the static call graph sees the registrations but not the per-record callbacks the framework invokes at runtime (ValueMapper.apply, ValueTransformer.transform, ProcessorSupplier.get, etc.).\n\nScope: a kafka_streams_dispatch.py linker (or an extension of message_dispatch.py) that:\n1. Recognises ValueMapper / ValueTransformer / ProcessorSupplier / KeyValueMapper / Predicate / ForeachAction / TransformerSupplier / Aggregator / Reducer / Initializer / Merger base types from org.apache.kafka.streams.kstream\n2. For each concrete impl, marks the framework-called methods (apply, transform, process, get, init, close) as reachable from the enclosing topology-builder call-site via framework_dispatches_to edges\n3. Does the same for the .streams-scala wrapper types used by Scala consumers\n\nCross-language relevance: Kafka topologies cross language boundaries via Kafka records. SerDe classes (Serializer.serialize / Deserializer.deserialize) are also dispatched this way and could share machinery.\n\nAcceptance: re-run of dead-code-prospector shows kafka_streams_internal drops below 800 (67% reduction)."  # 0731
    fields: {}  # 0731
- op: discuss  # 40b6
  at: '2026-04-16T19:36:54Z'  # 40b6
  by: agent  # 40b6
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 40b6
  clock: 2  # 40b6
  nonce: 40b6  # 40b6
  message: "Clarification on cross-languageness: the phrase 'cross-language via Kafka record SerDe boundary' in the original description overstated this item's scope. The linker itself operates entirely within Java/Scala source — Kafka Streams' topology builder registers ValueMapper/ValueTransformer/ProcessorSupplier impls at build time, and the runtime dispatches the callbacks (apply/transform/process/get/init) per record. The cross-language consequence (Kafka records flow to consumers in Python/Go/Node) is real but downstream of the linker; it's the message_queue.py / message_dispatch.py class of edge, not this one.\n\nCorrect framing: this is a within-JVM framework-dispatch linker for Kafka Streams topology registration. If we ever want true cross-language edges along the Kafka record path, that's a separate item for a Kafka-topic → consumer-class linker that could reuse SerDe fingerprints across languages."  # 40b6
